• penalties;
• refusal of the FDA to review pending market approval applications or supplements to approval applications;
• total or partial suspension of production;
• civil penalties;
• withdrawals of previously approved marketing applications; and
• criminal prosecutions.
The regulatory review and approval process is lengthy, expensive and uncertain. Before obtaining regulatory approvals for the commercial sale of any
products, we or our partners must demonstrate that our product candidates are safe and effective for use in humans. The approval process takes many years,
substantial expenses may be incurred and significant time may be devoted to clinical development.
